# Architecture Rules

## Product Shape

- This repository is a native macOS software steward app. The supported app entry is SwiftUI + AppKit under `native/MacSoftwareSteward/`.
- There is no Xcode project. Build, test, packaging, and release flows are driven by shell scripts and direct `xcrun swiftc` invocations.
- Do not reintroduce the old web panel as a supported runtime path unless the task explicitly asks for that migration.

## Main Modules

- `native/MacSoftwareSteward/App.swift` owns the app entry point, windows, menu bar integration, command menus, and top-level environment object injection.
- `native/MacSoftwareSteward/ContentView.swift` owns top-level navigation and page containment.
- `native/MacSoftwareSteward/Views/*.swift` owns SwiftUI pages and shared UI components.
- `native/MacSoftwareSteward/Models.swift` owns shared scan, package, job, update, and policy data models.
- `native/MacSoftwareSteward/StewardModel.swift` is the main `@MainActor ObservableObject` view model. Keep new logic out of this file when a focused pure helper or store can hold it instead.
- `native/MacSoftwareSteward/Scanner.swift` owns Applications, Homebrew, and `mas` scanning and parsing.
- `native/MacSoftwareSteward/CommandRunner.swift` owns process execution, timeout handling, streaming output, and PATH fallback.
- `native/MacSoftwareStewardAgent/AgentMain.swift` is a non-GUI helper for `daily-check`; it must avoid SwiftUI/AppKit dependencies.

## Persistence And Automation

- Local app state lives under `~/Library/Application Support/MacSoftwareSteward/` through focused JSON stores such as `AutomationProfileStore`, `InboxStore`, `InspectionReportStore`, `UpgradePolicyStore`, and `UpgradeHistoryStore`.
- Daily inspection is scheduled through a user LaunchAgent generated by `DailyInspectionScheduler`.
- Background agent outcomes should be represented as local reports and Inbox items where practical, not only as text logs.
- App self-update must keep SHA-256 verification and rollback behavior intact.

## Build And Release Contracts

- `npm test` runs `bash scripts/test-native.sh`.
- `npm run build` runs `bash scripts/build-native.sh`.
- `npm run package` runs `bash scripts/package-release.sh`.
- `npm run release` runs `bash scripts/release-github.sh`.
- `scripts/build-native.sh` generates AppIcon iconset PNGs as part of the build. If a task does not intentionally change app icons, restore `native/Resources/AppIcon.iconset/*.png` after building.
- Local output directories `build/`, `release/`, and `code-risk-scanner/` are generated or local analysis artifacts and should not be committed.

## Versioning

- When changing the app version, keep `package.json` `version` and `native/Info.plist` `CFBundleShortVersionString` / `CFBundleVersion` in sync.

## Dependency Boundaries

- Main app code may use SwiftUI and AppKit.
- Agent code must remain command-line friendly and must not depend on GUI frameworks.
- Homebrew is recommended, `mas` is optional, and the app should degrade gracefully when either tool is unavailable.
- Finder/Dock launches do not load shell profile PATH. Use existing `CommandRunner` PATH fallback patterns instead of assuming shell environment setup.
